{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793887089,"nonce":"4MXZbr5Oi2qyX0KXlglHEor8XGI=","title":"Defer scalar-replacement use indexes until local escape checks pass","message":"Follow-up to 1be184c and 7e6293fc7ee6d50a46b92ca277ea3363d873f81d: candidate-free guards remove unused analysis, but hot main bodies still contain mallocs. scalar_replace_alloc eagerly builds BlockUses even when each candidate escapes through a local call, instruction, phi or terminator.\n\nBuild the index only after local candidate checks succeed, reuse while the function is unchanged, and invalidate after scalar replacement rather than immediately rebuild. Preserve global checks of instructions, indirect callees, terminators, phi inputs and pointer-integer aliases. Validate load forwarding that exposes cross-block pointer uses, allocation growth for locally rejected candidates, optimized HIR, full pinned TS corpus and Lua/Python conformance. Compare frozen baseline/candidate binaries on an idle NUC with snapshots enabled and LLVM off.","files":null}]}